From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:27:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #3875] Re-enable the bug-3873 test for mcs51

The test passes with --model-medium, --model-large, --model-huge and both
stack-auto variants on current trunk, so whatever made it fail has been
fixed since. It stays disabled only for the plain small model, where its
data does not fit into internal RAM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 support/regression/tests/bug-3873.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/support/regression/tests/bug-3873.c b/support/regression/tests/bug-3873.c
index 8b15ff2fe..ba3d5d037 100644
--- a/support/regression/tests/bug-3873.c
+++ b/support/regression/tests/bug-3873.c
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ static void huffCreate(const uint8* pBits, HuffTable* pHuffTable)
 }
 
 void testBug(void) {
-#ifndef __SDCC_mcs51 // Bug #3875
+#if !(defined(__SDCC_mcs51) && defined(__SDCC_MODEL_SMALL) && !defined(__SDCC_STACK_AUTO)) // Lack of memory
     huffCreate(gBits, &gHuffTab0);
 
     ASSERT(gHuffTab0.mMinCode[0] == 0x0000);
